## Why This Problem Is Asked
This classic problem evaluates your ability to design clean DP states for interval selection with reconstruction requirements. It strikes the right balance—accessible to beginners while effectively testing state structuring and backtracking skills.

## Key Concepts
- **dp[i][t]** manages selections across the first i elements with at most t subarrays
- **local[i][t]** distinguishes between extending an existing subarray and starting a new one
- Backtracking through the DP table to reconstruct segment boundaries

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxSumSubarrays(nums, k) {
    if (!nums.length || k <= 0) return { maxSum: 0, subarrays: [] };

    const n = nums.length;
    const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(0));
    const local = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(0));
    const endIdx = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-1));

    for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
        for (let t = 1; t <= Math.min(k, i); t++) {
            local[i][t] = Math.max(
                local[i - 1][t] + nums[i - 1],
                dp[i - 1][t - 1] + nums[i - 1]
            );
            if (local[i][t] === dp[i - 1][t - 1] + nums[i - 1]) {
                endIdx[i][t] = i - 1;
            }
            dp[i][t] = dp[i - 1][t] >= local[i][t] ? dp[i - 1][t] : local[i][t];
        }
    }

    const subarrays = [];
    let j = n, t = k;
    while (t > 0 && j > 0) {
        if (endIdx[j][t] !== -1) {
            let start = endIdx[j][t];
            while (start > 0 && endIdx[start][t] !== -1) start--;
            subarrays.unshift([start, endIdx[j][t]]);
            j = start;
            t--;
        } else {
            break;
        }
    }

    return { maxSum: dp[n][k], subarrays };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests dynamic programming over non-overlapping subarrays where block value depends on internal structure, requiring precomputation and reconstruction techniques.

## Key Concepts

- Non-overlapping k blocks in increasing order
- Precomputation of per-block value (peaks inside)
- DP with inner maximization over l
- Reconstruction pointers; time/space trade-offs

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxValueSubarrays(A, k, F, P) {
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) pref[i+1] = pref[i] + A[i];
  const peaks = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));

  // Precompute peaks
  for (let i = 1; i < n-1; i++) {
    if (A[i-1] < A[i] && A[i] > A[i+1]) {
      for (let l = 0; l <= i; l++) {
        for (let r = i; r < n; r++) {
          peaks[l][r]++;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  const val = (l, r) => pref[r+1] - pref[l] - F - P * peaks[l][r];

  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const parent = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));

  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t];
      for (let l = 1; l <= i; l++) {
        if (dp[l-1][t-1] + val(l-1, i-1) > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = dp[l-1][t-1] + val(l-1, i-1);
          parent[i][t] = l-1;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct
  const blocks = [];
  let cur = n, curT = k;
  while (curT > 0 && parent[cur][curT] !== -1) {
    const start = parent[cur][curT];
    blocks.unshift([start, cur-1]);
    cur = start;
    curT--;
  }

  return { max: dp[n][k], blocks };
}
```

## Complexity

- Time: O(n²k) due to nested loops for peaks, DP, and reconstruction
- Space: O(nk) for DP table and parent pointers, reducible to O(n) with rolling arrays

The key challenge is efficiently computing block values while maintaining optimal substructure across k non-overlapping segments.

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP over prefixes with a non-linear subarray cost (max) and requires reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP over prefixes and partition count
- On-the-fly max for subarray cost
- Reconstruction via prev pointers
- Time/space trade-offs (O(n^2 k) time, O(nk) space)

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostPartition(A, k){
  const n = A.length;
  const INF = 1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(INF));
  const prev = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1; i<=n; i++){
    for(let t=1; t<=Math.min(i,k); t++){
      let curMax = -Infinity;
      for(let p=i-1; p>=t-1; p--){
        curMax = Math.max(curMax, A[p]);
        const val = dp[p][t-1] + curMax;
        if(val < dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; prev[i][t] = p; }
      }
    }
  }
  return {cost: dp[n][k], prev};
}
```

